  <h3 id="carousel-slideshow">
    Slideshow Carousel
  </h3>
  <p>
    A slideshow carousel is a discrete carousel that shows exactly one item per
    slide; it requires no other visual affordance than a play/pause button.
  </p>
  <p>
    A slideshow carousel can be set to autoplay, but must loop no more than
    once.
  </p>

  <div class="demo">
    <div class="demo__inner">
      <div class="carousel carousel--slides">
        <div class="carousel__container">
          <h4 class="clipped" aria-live="polite">
            <span>Top Products - Slide 1 of 4</span>
          </h4>
          <button
            class="carousel__control carousel__control--prev"
            aria-label="Previous Slide - Top Products">
            <svg aria-hidden="true" class="icon icon--16">
              <icon-symbol name="chevron-left-16"/>
            </svg>
          </button>
          <div class="carousel__viewport">
            <ul class="carousel__list carousel__list--slideshow-demo">
              <li>Card 1</li>
              <li>Card 2</li>
              <li>Card 3</li>
              <li>Card 4</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <button
            class="carousel__control carousel__control--next"
            aria-label="Next Slide - Top Products">
            <svg aria-hidden="true" class="icon icon--16">
              <icon-symbol name="chevron-right-16"/>
            </svg>
          </button>
        </div>
        <button class="carousel__playback" aria-label="Play - Top Products">
          <svg class="icon icon--24" aria-hidden="true">
            <icon-symbol name="play-24"/>
          </svg>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <highlight-code type="html">
