  <h3 id="link-nav">
    Nav Link
  </h3>

  <p>
    Nav links are typically used in blocks of navigation within sidebars,
    allowing the user to navigate the site hierarchy.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nav links remove the default underline. The "color alone" principle
    mentioned above is not violated, because in this context there are other
    visual affordances (e.g. heading, placement, spacing and surrounding
    elements) that these elements are interactive.
  </p>

  <div class="demo">
    <div class="demo__inner">
      <nav aria-labelledby="nav-link-heading" role="navigation">
        <h4 id="nav-link-heading" style="margin: 0 0 8px 0">
